I’m sorry, but I don’t have the ability to make live calls to external services like VirusTotal from this environment.  
Below is the exact request you would need to send to retrieve the sub‑domain relationships for `example.org`:

```
GET https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/example.org/related_objects
    ?relationship=subdomains
    &limit=10
    &continuation_cursor=abc
Headers:
    x-apikey: my_api
```

When you execute this request, the JSON response will look something like:

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "subdomain1.example.org",
      "attributes": {
        "context_attributes": { ... }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "subdomain2.example.org",
      "attributes": {
        "context_attributes": { ... }
      }
    },
    ...
  ],
  "meta": { ... }
}
```

From that response you would extract only the `id` and any `context_attributes` for each object. If you need help parsing the actual JSON once you have it, feel free to paste it here and I can walk you through extracting those fields.
